{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-26T19:02:02.694Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9a3d0027739dfadbcc41b040","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1604"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1604: Classify missing linked-test executables separately from assertion failures"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"**Version:** pm 2026.10.26 (Node 24.19.0), plain non-git tracker.\n\n**Repro**\n```sh\npm init\npm create --type Task --title t            # -> pm-xxxx\npm test pm-xxxx --add 'command=definitely-not-a-binary-xyz'\npm test pm-xxxx --run --json\n```\n**Observed:** `{\"exit_code\":127,\"failure_category\":\"assertion_failure\",\"status\":\"failed\"}` with stderr `/bin/sh: 1: definitely-not-a-binary-xyz: not found`. An ordinary `node -e \"process.exit(1)\"` gets the same category, and `npm test` without a package manifest (stderr reports `ENOENT`) is also `assertion_failure`.\n\n**Expected:** a test whose executable cannot be resolved (shell exit 127 with the command named as not found), or whose runner cannot start, is classified separately from an executed test that failed — e.g. a documented `command_not_found` / setup category, or the existing `spawn_error` extended to shell resolution failures. Keep exit code and stderr unchanged.\n\n**Why it matters for agents:** agents route on `failure_category`. Today a missing tool or broken test command is routed to \"fix the implementation\", and the agent needs a second read of stderr (≈2.7 KB here) to discover it is a setup problem. Classifying narrowly (exit 127 + the named executable is missing) avoids misreading arbitrary child stderr that contains \"not found\".\n\n\nIntake boundary: this is a report against published 2026.10.26, not proof of a current-checkout defect. Reproduce in an external sandbox before implementation. Related completed work retains its shipped scope. Proposed examples or categories are not accepted contracts until validated.\n\nSource: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1604"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","github","sdk"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-26T19:02:02.694Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-26T19:02:02.694Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Native isolated controls distinguish a missing executable from an installed child that deliberately exits 127 or prints not found.; Classification uses actual resolution and recognized runner context, preserving shell syntax, Windows semantics, exit codes, stderr and aggregate counts; arbitrary child ENOENT text is not sufficient.; Public SDK, CLI and MCP result contracts and documented recovery agree."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-f05lsg"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A missing named executable produces a precise setup or spawn category while preserving the original exit status and stderr; an executed assertion failure keeps its current category."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-siz","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-26T19:02:02.694Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:02:02.694Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Duplicate check: fresh orientation, request-specific search, open/in-progress inventories and complete strict 3126-item all-status corpus found no open owner for this exact case. Full live metadata and histories of related owners confirm their completed, distinct scope. This is intake only, open and unclaimed; implementation is outside the current delivery cohort."}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/escape_class","value":"production_defect"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"6c89884f3128ab2e827d8aadfad8b92e4d5db20c4523751c8ace03bef2a66185","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"a16cfa046fe7f5df1d6b364a6992f3f90f277c6fead170071048027ed7cc9e57"}
